        <field>Body__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">In 1911 more than a million people in Austria, Denmark, Germany, and Switzerland rallied for women's right to vote, to work, and to hold office. On March 8, 1917, women textile workers in Petrograd, Russia, walked out demanding bread and peace, and their strike set the date. The UN began marking the day in 1975.</value>
